    thinking: "**Discovering Image Assets**\n\nI\'ve uncovered a few SVG images \342\200\223 personalTesting.png, running.png, and yoga.png \342\200\223 which are pretty interesting. I\'m noting that running.png is definitely the same image as a previously observed asset.\n\n\n**Analyzing Image Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how Next.js handles SVG files disguised as `.png` files. I realized that the previous developer likely included `NextImageShim.tsx` to handle this exact situation. It seems the issue is due to Next.js\'s image optimization process, specifically when it tries to process a file that isn\'t a standard PNG. Setting `unoptimized: true` in `next.config.mjs` prevents this, passing the SVG to the browser directly. Creating `src/components/NextImage.tsx` will be essential for managing image imports.\n\n\n**Investigating Image Import**\n\nI\'m now diving into the purpose of `import Image from \"next/image\"`. I\'m exploring the idea of a custom image wrapper or alias, and the possibilities for using Next.js\'s built-in `Image` component with `unoptimized: true`. I\'m curious about how browsers handle SVGs served as `.png` files, and if that impacts rendering quality, and I\'m comparing this to the direct SVG rendering of `NextImageShim`. I\'m looking closely at `NextImageShim.tsx` to get a better handle on the images it\'s using.\n\n\n"
