  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing the Server Output**\n\nI\'m currently watching the server\'s output, noting the Next.js version (16.3.8 with Turbopack). I see it\'s running locally on port 3000, and it\'s compiled and ready in just over a second. The HEAD request returned a 200 status after 8.9 seconds. I\'m focusing on those metrics for a baseline.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Command Flow**\n\nI\'ve traced the execution path and identified the root cause: the `control-plane-api` is passing `--host=0.0.0.0` to Next.js\'s dev server, which it doesn\'t support, causing a crash. This happens when `restart_dev_server` is called. To verify, I\'m building a simple `dev-server.js` script to clean the unsupported flags before passing them to the Next.js process, which I believe will resolve the error and allow the server to restart correctly.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_257394"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env node\\nimport { spawn } from \'child_process\';\\n\\nconst args = [\'dev\', \'-p\', \'3000\', \'-H\', \'0.0.0.0\'];\\n\\nconst child = spawn(\'npx\', [\'next\', ...args], {\\n  stdio: \'inherit\',\\n  env: process.env,\\n});\\n\\nchild.on(\'exit\', (code) => {\\n  process.exit(code ?? 0);\\n});\\n\\nprocess.on(\'SIGTERM\', () => child.kill(\'SIGTERM\'));\\nprocess.on(\'SIGINT\', () => child.kill(\'SIGINT\'));\\n\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/dev-server.js\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating dev-server.js wrapper\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create dev-server.js wrapper\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "create_file"
    }
