flow-visible` properties interact within these specific `div` and `h1` elements. I believe the new `z-30` added to the `h1` will give this priority. The new code blocks have increased visibility across containers, aiming for a cleaner visual representation. I\'m especially interested in the implications for the text rendering, given the absolute positioning and the various `z-index` levels now in play. I\'m working on the interaction of the text with potential overlapping elements.\n\n\n**Optimizing Text Styling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the text styling for \"POWER YOUR PONTETIALE.\" I\'m examining the effects of `-webkit-text-stroke` in both inline styles and global CSS, comparing the results of direct application with utility classes. I need to make sure the font, size, and particularly the text stroke, render consistently and correctly to ensure the desired visual effect is achieved, especially now that I\'m also adding `color: transparent`.\n\n\n"
